.TH "CSVJOIN" "1" "Aug 16, 2024" "2.2.0" "csvkit"
.SH NAME
csvjoin \- csvjoin Documentation
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Merges two or more CSV tables together using a method analogous to SQL JOIN operation. By default it performs an inner join, but full outer, left outer, and right outer are also available via flags. Key columns are specified with the \-c flag (either a single column which exists in all tables, a \(dq+\(dq\-separated list of columns to join on a composite key, or a comma\-separated list of such specifications with one corresponding to each file). Rows in which any part of the key is null never match. If the columns flag is not provided then the tables will be merged \(dqsequentially\(dq, that is they will be merged in row order with no filtering:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
usage: csvjoin [\-h] [\-d DELIMITER] [\-t] [\-q QUOTECHAR] [\-u {0,1,2,3}] [\-b]
               [\-p ESCAPECHAR] [\-z FIELD_SIZE_LIMIT] [\-e ENCODING] [\-L LOCALE]
               [\-S] [\-\-blanks] [\-\-null\-value NULL_VALUES [NULL_VALUES ...]]
               [\-\-date\-format DATE_FORMAT] [\-\-datetime\-format DATETIME_FORMAT]
               [\-H] [\-K SKIP_LINES] [\-v] [\-l] [\-\-zero] [\-V] [\-c COLUMNS]
               [\-\-outer] [\-\-left] [\-\-right] [\-\-right\-unique]
               [\-y SNIFF_LIMIT] [\-I] [FILE [FILE ...]]

Execute a SQL\-like join to merge CSV files on a specified column or columns.

positional arguments:
  FILE                  The CSV files to operate on. If only one is specified,
                        it will be copied to STDOUT.

optional arguments:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit
  \-c COLUMNS, \-\-columns COLUMNS
                        The column name(s) on which to join. To join on a
                        composite key, separate the names (or indices) with
                        \(dq+\(dq, for example \(dqregion+store\(dq. To use
                        different columns in each file, provide a
                        comma\-separated list with one such specification per
                        file, in the same order in which the files were
                        specified. If not specified, the two files will be
                        joined sequentially without matching.
  \-\-outer               Perform a full outer join, rather than the default
                        inner join.
  \-\-left                Perform a left outer join, rather than the default
                        inner join. If more than two files are provided this
                        will be executed as a sequence of left outer joins,
                        starting at the left.
  \-\-right               Perform a right outer join, rather than the default
                        inner join. If more than two files are provided this
                        will be executed as a sequence of right outer joins,
                        starting at the right.
  \-\-right\-unique        Require that each join key appears in at most one
                        row of every right\-hand file. If any key is
                        duplicated, the duplicated keys are reported and no
                        output is written.
  \-y SNIFF_LIMIT, \-\-snifflimit SNIFF_LIMIT
                        Limit CSV dialect sniffing to the specified number of
                        bytes. Specify \(dq0\(dq to disable sniffing entirely, or
                        \(dq\-1\(dq to sniff the entire file.
  \-I, \-\-no\-inference    Disable type inference (and \-\-locale, \-\-date\-format,
                        \-\-datetime\-format, \-\-no\-leading\-zeroes) when parsing
                        the input.

Note that the join operation requires reading all files into memory. Don\(aqt try
this on very large files.
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: \fI\%Arguments common to all tools\fP\&.
.SH EXAMPLES
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
csvjoin \-c 1 examples/join_a.csv examples/join_b.csv
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Join on a composite key (a store is identified by its region and store number together), requiring the right\-hand file to have at most one row per key:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
csvjoin \-c region+store \-\-right\-unique examples/join_composite_details.csv examples/join_composite_stores.csv
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Add two empty columns to the right of a CSV:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
echo \(dq,\(dq | csvjoin examples/dummy.csv \-
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Add a single column to the right of a CSV:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
echo \(dqnew\-column\(dq | csvjoin examples/dummy.csv \-
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
